{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1967"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge nature/mammals","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/zz-r2-nature__mammals.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",966],["-","Henning the rooster, "],["=",13],["+"," From the farmyard come a pair of names that often appear together: Adelheid (or Alheid) and Henning are the goose and rooster of the fable – Henning the cock opens Goethe's epic by bringing the king the body of his daughter, killed by Reineke."],["=",126],["+","\n| Adelheid / Henning | goose / rooster | farmyard victims of the fox |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",906],["-","Henning der Hahn, "],["=",13],["+"," Aus dem Hühnerhof stammt ein Namenspaar, das oft zusammen genannt wird: Adelheid (oder Alheid) und Henning sind Gans und Hahn der Fabel – Henning, der Hahn, eröffnet Goethes Epos, indem er dem König den Leichnam seiner von Reineke getöteten Tochter bringt."],["=",124],["+","\n| Adelheid / Henning | Gans / Hahn | Opfer des Fuchses aus dem Hühnerhof |"]]}]},
